  "title": "The community built more than image generators",
  "summary": "October made Pollinations easier to build with: more community apps, broader model choices, simpler API access, and clearer Pollen accounting.\n\nHacktoberfest and other submissions filled the project directory with design tools, agents, games, bots, and mobile apps, including AI Packaging Designer and ReImagine. An app registry and deployment workflow added a path for hosting Hacktoberfest projects on Pollinations subdomains.\n\nThe model lineup gained Claude Haiku 4.5 and Seedream 4.0, while gptimage returned for generation and editing and gained a high-quality Nectar option. Seedream’s image budget grew, and Nano Banana gained image-to-image support through Enter.\n\nImage-model listings and metadata became available through dedicated endpoints. Bearer authentication, browser preflight support, a GET text endpoint, and copyable publishable keys made common requests easier to wire up; the API guide gained fuller text, image, and audio examples.\n\nEnter’s dashboard and FAQ made balances, keys, model access, and Pollen rules easier to read. Its subscription panel now distinguishes an assigned tier from an active Polar subscription and reads active product details from Polar.",
